From d4d2f41378af586d02a51ce8a97f34df15d75b55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mate Soos <soos.mate@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:10:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix crash on an empty input clause

Bug: a clause line consisting only of "0" is the empty clause, so the
formula is trivially UNSAT, but xorcle crashes on it: the release build
segfaults, the debug build fails "Assertion `clause.rows() >= 1'" in
PropagationEngine::unit_prop_one_clause (src/search/PropagationEngine.cpp:33).
Propagation assumes every clause has at least one row. Reproducer:

  p xnf 2 2
  1 2 0
  0

Fix: solve() looks for an empty input clause before propagating and returns
UNSAT right away. With a proof requested it logs the empty clause with that
input clause as its only reason, which tools/check_drup_parity.py accepts.

Found with hand-written edge cases next to differential fuzzing
(xnf_fuzzer.py).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/search/Solver.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/search/Solver.cpp b/src/search/Solver.cpp
index bc255c2..0a8f4ad 100644
--- a/src/search/Solver.cpp
+++ b/src/search/Solver.cpp
@@ -367,6 +367,17 @@ void Solver::make_decision_step() {
 Result Solver::solve() {
     next_proof_clause_id = std::max(next_proof_clause_id, clause_sel->get_num_clauses());
 
+    // propagation assumes every clause has a row, so an empty input clause must be caught here
+    const std::vector<algebra::Clause>& clauses = get_clauses();
+    for (heuristics::ClauseId id = 0; id < clauses.size(); ++id) {
+        if (clauses[id].rows() == 0) {
+            if (proof_logger) {
+                proof_logger->log_empty_clause(next_proof_clause_id++, {id});
+            }
+            return ResultCase::Unsat {};
+        }
+    }
+
     while (true) {
         if (propagate_until_conflict()) {
             ++num_conflicts;
